  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "P001",
      "FreFlow",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P002",
      "5\nMaintenance\n5.1\nDaily maintenance\nRegularly check the outlet pressure.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P003",
      "(cid:2)\nNo water should get into the terminal box of the electric motor when the\npump room is sprayed clean!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P004",
      "Never spray water on hot pump parts!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P005",
      "The\nsudden cooling down may cause them to burst and hot water may flow out!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P006",
      "!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P007",
      "Flawed maintenance will result in shorter lifespan, possible break down and\nin any event loss of warranty.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P008",
      "5.2\nCombustion engine\n(cid:2)\nNever top up with fuel while the motor is running!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P009",
      "5.3\nMechanical seal\n• A mechanical seal generally requires no maintenance, however, it should never be\nallowed to run dry.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P010",
      "So the oil chamber behind the mechanical seal must always be\nfilled with a lubricating liquid which will not attack the liquid to be pumped nor the\nmechanical seal.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P011",
      "See paragraph 10.1 \"Oil chamber\" for the appropriate oil type.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P012",
      "• Drain the oil or the liquid every 2000 hours of operation or once a year and replace it\nby fresh oil or liquid.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P013",
      "For the recommanded quantities see paragraph 10.1 \"Oil\nchamber\".",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P014",
      "➢\nMake sure the drained oil or liquid is discharged safely.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P015",
      "See to it that it doesn’t get into\nthe environment.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P016",
      "• If there are no problems it is not advisable to dismantle the seal.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P017",
      "As the facing surfaces\nare running in on one another.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P018",
      "Dismantling always means replacement of the\nmechanical seal.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P019",
      "When the shaft seal is leaking it has to be replaced.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P020",
      "!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P021",
      "If the mechanical seal should start to leak, the oil chamber will overflow via\nthe hole in the oil filler cap and the pump must be immediately stopped to\nreplace the mechanical seal!",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P022",
      "5.4\nDouble mechanical seal\nRegularly check the pressure of the flushing liquid.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P023",
      "This pressure must be 1,5 bar\nhigher than the pressure at the impeller hub.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P024",
      "Maintenance\n27\nFRE/EN (2502) 9.7",
      false,
      "prose",
      "29:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P025",
      "5.5\nEnvironmental influences\n• Regularly clean the filter in the suction pipe or the suction strainer at the bottom of the\nsuction pipe, as the inlet pressure may become too low if the filter or the suction\nstrainer is fouled.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P026",
      "• If there is a risk that the pumped liquid expands during solidification or freezing, the\npump has to be drained and, if necessary, flushed after it has been put out of service.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P027",
      "• If the pump is out of service for a long time, it has to be preserved.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P028",
      "• Check motor for accumulation of dust or dirt, which might influence motor\ntemperature.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P029",
      "5.6\nNoise\nIf a pump starts making noise, this may point to certain problems with the pump unit.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P030",
      "A\ncrackling noise can indicate cavitation or excessive motor noise can indicate\ndeterioration of the bearings.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P031",
      "5.7\nMotor\nCheck motor specifications for start-stop frequency.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P032",
      "5.8\nFaults\n(cid:2)\nThe pump, of which you want to determine the fault, may be hot or under\npressure.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P033",
      "Take the appropriate precautions first and protect yourself with\nthe proper safety devices (safety goggles, gloves, protective clothing)!",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P034",
      "To determine the source of the malfunctioning of the pump, proceed as follows:",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P035",
      "1 Switch off the power supply to the pump unit.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P036",
      "Lock the working switch with a padlock\nor remove the fuse.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P037",
      "In case of a combustion engine: switch off the engine and close\nthe fuel supply to the engine.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P038",
      "2 Close the stop valves.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P039",
      "3 Determine the nature of the fault.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P040",
      "4 Try to determine the cause of the fault with chapter 6 \"Problem solving\" and take the\nappropriate measures or contact your installer.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P041",
      "28\nMaintenance\nFRE/EN (2502) 9.7",
      true,
      "prose",
      "30:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ]
  ],
